  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-voice-input-qwen-asr",
      "text": "[简体中文](./README.zh.md) · English\n\nA [DeepSeek Harness (DSH)](../deepseek-harness) dual-face plugin that adds **voice input** to the chat composer: a mic button next to the send action, a live recording bubble, and a local **Qwen3-ASR** inference service managed entirely by the host."
    },
    {
      "section": "Demo",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"assets/demo/asr-demo.mp4\">\n    <img src=\"assets/demo/asr-demo-poster.jpg\" alt=\"Voice input demo (15s)\" width=\"800\" />\n  </a>\n</p>\n\n*▶ Click the frame to play on GitHub (opens the built-in video player) · or [download the clip](assets/demo/asr-demo.mp4).*"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Mic button** — registered into the `conversation.input.right` slot, rendered on the left of the composer's send button. Click to start, click again (or press \"Done, insert\") to stop.\n- **Recording bubble** — a portal-anchored bubble with a pulsing indicator, RMS-driven wave bars, elapsed time, and the live partial transcript streamed back from ASR.\n- **Real-time streaming** — the browser captures 16 kHz PCM16 mono via AudioWorklet and pushes chunks over a host-relayed WebSocket (`/api/dsh-voice-input-qwen-asr.ws`) to the local ASR service; partial transcripts stream back in real time.\n- **Local ASR service** — the host half spawns `python/asr_server.py` with the runtime virtualenv's Python. The server loads `Qwen3-ASR-0.6B` (transformers backend, CUDA when available) and serves a WebSocket transcription endpoint.\n- **Environment setup page** — a `settings.section` page (\"Voice\") that clones the runtime repo and model repo, creates a Python virtualenv inside the runtime directory, installs dependencies, starts/stops the service, and streams install/server logs."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- DSH host with `webServer` + `connection` services (web profile)\n- `git` (and **git-lfs** — model weights are distributed via LFS)\n- Python **3.12+** (on `PATH`, or an absolute path configured in settings)\n- Optional: NVIDIA GPU + CUDA for fast inference; CPU fallback works but is slow"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-voice-input-qwen-asr   # or npm name / .tgz / github:you/repo#sha\ndsh --profile web --dump-config                  # verify the layer\ndsh --profile web                                # restart the host\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "1. Open **Settings → Voice**, press **Install all** (or run the four steps individually): clone runtime → clone model → create virtualenv → install deps. Watch the install log; the deps step downloads torch and may take a while. `pip` mirror can be configured on the same page.\n2. Press **Start service** and wait until the state chip turns \"Running\" (device shows `cuda:0` or `cpu`).\n3. In any chat, click the mic button left of the send button, speak, then press **Done, insert** — the recognized text is appended to the input draft. \"Cancel\" discards the recording."
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "```\nbrowser                          host (Node)                      local python\n┌─────────────────┐   POST /dsh-voice-input-qwen-asr/api   ┌──────────────┐\n│ mic button      │ ────────────────────────────▶ │ ops: status  │\n│ bubble (portal) │                               │ install / sv │"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "- `src/host/` — cordis plugin: HTTP API route (trust-fenced), WebSocket upgrade route (connection-service auth), installer (git clone / venv / pip), ASR process manager, relay hub, JSON store at `$DSH_HOME/dsh-voice-input-qwen-asr.json`.\n- `src/client/` — browser plugin: `conversation.input.right` + `settings.section` slots, i18n (zh/en), styles, mic capture, WS client.\n- `python/asr_server.py` — asyncio + `websockets` server; buffers incoming PCM, periodically transcribes a tail window for partials, transcribes the full buffer on `stop`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Build",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm run check    # tsc -b (host + client programs)\npnpm run build    # → lib/index.js (node) + lib/client.js (browser factory)\npnpm run verify   # simulate host module loader, assert factory shape"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
